<title>CANADA: Bank of Canada 91-day T-bill yields avg 3.036 pct.</title>
<headline>Bank of Canada 91-day T-bill yields avg 3.036 pct.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Canada said the average yield at this week's auction of C$2.4 billion of 91-day Government of Canada treasury bills due March 20, 1997 was 3.036 percent, up from 2.856 percent last week.</p>
<p>The average yield on C$1.4 billion of 182-day T-bills due June 19, 1997 was 3.379 percent, up from 3.130 percent last week, and on C$1.0 billion of 357-day T-bills due December 11, 1997 was 3.812 percent, up from 3.424 percent.</p>
<p>The Bank bought C$700 million three-month, C$225 million six-month and C$150 million one-year bills. It holds C$1.1 billion of C$7.0 billion bills due next week.</p>
